# Rank 1115 / CVE-2023-4005: FOSSBilling's password-change endpoint verified
# the current password and updated it, but left every other active session
# for that account untouched, so a session an attacker had already stolen
# stayed valid after the legitimate user "secured" the account by changing
# its password (CWE-613).
#
# Client::change_password in src/modules/Profile/Api/Client.php verified
# `current_password` against the stored hash and called
# `changeClientPassword()`, with nothing in between that touched any session
# record. The password itself was rotated; nothing else was.
#
# Pool commit 20c23b051eb6 is the real fix (COMMIT_OK, GHSA-vq32-qxmx-986v).
# It adds Service::invalidateSessions(), which reads every row from the
# `session` table, decodes each one to check whether it belongs to the
# account being changed, and deletes the matches, and calls it from
# change_password (both Client and Admin APIs) before the password update
# runs, plus a new destroy_sessions API action a user can call directly. No
# pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, vocabulary gap. Scanning either revision reports 0 findings.
# code.MissingSessionRotationAfterAuthentication is the nearest concept,
# already used at rank 1110 for the same reasoning: it carries CWE_384 rather
# than this CVE's CWE_613, and its reviewCondition, "authentication completes
# without rotating or invalidating the existing HTTP session", is written for
# the moment a session begins (login), not the moment a credential the user
# already trusts less changes (password reset). Both are "a security-relevant
# event should invalidate stale session state and doesn't", but the concept's
# only binding is Java's session.regenerateId() at login, with nothing about
# a change-password flow leaving sibling sessions alone. Stating the general
# condition, a credential-change endpoint completes without invalidating
# other active sessions for the same account, needs recognizing a
# "credential-change endpoint" as its own category distinct from login, which
# is judgement rather than a port.
#
# No definition change attempted.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap, both revisions rejected.

test "rank1115: the password is changed and no session is touched"
  lang php
  file src/modules/Profile/Api/Client.php
  reject_review code.MissingSessionRotationAfterAuthentication
  code
  ```
  class Client extends \Api_Abstract
  {
      public function change_password($data)
      {
          $client = $this->getIdentity();

          if (!$this->di['password']->verify($data['current_password'], $client->pass)) {
              throw new \Exception('Current password incorrect');
          }

          return $this->getService()->changeClientPassword($client, $data['new_password']);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1115: existing sessions are invalidated before the password is changed"
  lang php
  file src/modules/Profile/Api/Client.php
  reject_review code.MissingSessionRotationAfterAuthentication
  code
  ```
  class Client extends \Api_Abstract
  {
      public function change_password($data)
      {
          $client = $this->getIdentity();

          if (!$this->di['password']->verify($data['current_password'], $client->pass)) {
              throw new \Exception('Current password incorrect');
          }

          $this->getService()->invalidateSessions();
          return $this->getService()->changeClientPassword($client, $data['new_password']);
      }
  }
  ```
